Description

Max has N friends. He writes their names in a sheet of paper. He wishes to find how many of his friends have distinct names.

Two names A and B are similar, if by swapping any ith and jth index of A any number of times, such that (i + j) % 2 == 0, A becomes B.

Names are distinct if they are not similar.

For example, abcd and cdab are not distinct, since we can swap indices 0 and 2, and then indices 1 and 3, to make abcd become cdab.

Help Max find how many distinct names his friends have.

Input Format

The first line contains N denoting the number of friends Max has.

Next N lines contain non-empty strings of lowercase Latin letters.

Output Format

Output the only integer — the number of distinct names.

Constraints

1 ≤ N ≤ 10^5

1 ≤ |A| ≤ 10^6, where |A| is the length of any input string.

The sum of lengths of all N strings does not exceed 10^6.

Sample Input 1

2
abcd
cdab

Sample Output 1

1

Sample Input 2

5
eceald
grauhe
ealdec
begwid
gebdiw

Sample Output 2

3

Note

Eceald and Ealdec are similar. Begwid and Gebdiw are similar.



#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl

void solve() {
    int n;
    cin>>n;
    set<string>st;
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        string s;
        cin>>s;
        int idx = 0;
        string odd = "";
        string eve = "";
        while(idx < s.size())
        {
            eve += s[idx];
            idx += 2;
        }
        idx = 1;
        while(idx < s.size())
        {
            odd += s[idx];
            idx += 2;
        }
        sort(eve.begin(),eve.end());
        sort(odd.begin(),odd.end());
        string newstr = eve + '#' + odd;
        st.insert(newstr);
        
    }
    cout<<st.size();
    
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t = 1;
    //cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}
